    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0204" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg148"/>

                <head>No. 82.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cadwalader to Mr. Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 31,
                        1876</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 237.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 358, of the 1st
                    instant, relative to the National Evangelical Church of Germany, I have to state
                    that the report <pb facs="0205" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/> of Mr. Chapman Coleman
                    respecting the laws regulating that organization and the proposed changes
                    therein, which accompanied your dispatch, exhibits an intelligent investigation
                    which is deserving of commendation.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN L. CADWALADER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
